#
# This is a stereotype extensions file. By convention a stereotype 
# extensions file must be named the same as the schema file used for 
# the project under the ..\Schema directory but named with the 
# *.stereotype-extensions file extension. For example:
#
# C:\
# ├── CGMES-CIM16
# │   ├── .settings 
# │   ├── Documentation
# │   │   ├── Images      
# │   │   ├── Includes     
# │   │   ├── Styles     
# │   │   └── Themes     
# │   ├── Incremental
# │   ├── Instances
# │   ├── Profiles
# │   └── Schema
# │       ├── iec61970cim16v33c_DY_pack_fix_WITH_ENTSO-E_EXTENSIONS.qea   
# │       └── iec61970cim16v33c_DY_pack_fix_WITH_ENTSO-E_EXTENSIONS.stereotype-extensions 
# │             (either manually create or drop the above file into the \Schema folder within the CIMTool UI)
# ├── .asciidoctorconfig.adoc 
# ├── .cimtool-settings        
# ├── .copyright-multi-line  
# ├── .copyright-single-line  
# ├── .project  
# └── ...
#
# If this file exists in the same folder as the schema file when 
# performing a schema import or creating a new CIMTool project,  
# CIMTool will automatically import it at the same time. 
# 
# These stereotype extensions files are intended to be used with EA 
# project files such as .eap, .qea, and .feap files. They are designed
# to be used to add stereotypes that do not need to be in the UML
# but rather are to be used to annotate classes, attributes, etc. at the
# time of profiling. This can be particularly useful then for the purposes
# of documentation or within PlantUML diagrams. An example usage is in
# the profiling done as part of IEC 619706-452 Ed 3.0 where ShortCircuit
# and Operation profiles that be co-specified within a Core Equipment profile.
# In this scenario the ShortCircuit attributes can be annotated with a
# ShortCircuit stereotype during the creation of the profiles to denote
# which attributes are a part of ShortCircuit data. This then can be 
# used in generated asciidoc and displayed to an end user for a more
# meaningful representation. Such stereotypes also propogate into the 
# PlantUML diagrams that get generated.
#
# Important notes on the <stereotype>=<description> mappings below:
#
# STEREOTYPES:
# Based on UML 2.5 specifications, UML stereotypes are considered
# case-insensitive and should NOT contain spaces. Therefore, the 
# stereotypes in the below mapping may be expressed either in
# the form they appear in the UML (e.g. NC for network codes)
# or in lowercase. Either is treated the same in CIMTool.
#
# DESCRIPTIONS:
# Free form description of what the Stereotype is used for.
#
Operation=Stereotype used to annotate attributes defined as part of the Core Equipment Operations profile.
ShortCircuit=Stereotype used to annotate attributes defined as part of the Core Equipment ShortCircuit profile.

